## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design verifiable, privacy-preserving aggregation systems with end-to-end integrity guarantees using non-interactive zero-knowledge proofs. Candidates should outline the complete architecture, data flows, and anti-tampering mechanisms required for secure distributed computation.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-preserving aggregation with succinct non-interactive arguments of knowledge (SNARKs)
- Tamper-evident ledger chaining for auditability
- Replay protection through nonce management and commitment schemes
- Poisoning resistance in distributed share systems via consistency checks

## Code Example
```javascript
